{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917307-rough-2e-conversion-of-scelesti-mechanics-from-left-hand-path","id":917307,"title":"Rough 2E Conversion of Scelesti Mechanics from Left-Hand Path","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-19T06:01:38-07:00","id":917307,"title":"Rough 2E Conversion of Scelesti Mechanics from Left-Hand Path","content":"Worked these up to represent the other major ways mages can gain control of Paradox. The existing method of controlling Paradox from the corebook is included for completion's sake.<br /> <br /> <b>Antinomian Imagos</b> - Any mage can invite Paradox into a spell, though doing so is highly addictive.. He doesn\u2019t contest the Paradox roll for a casting, but rolls Gnosis. Each success allows him to control one Reach applied by the Paradox roll.<br /> <br /> Next are the conversions. I haven't included information on how you unlock these, as that information is all included in Left-Hand path and doesn't need to be revised.<br /> <br /> <b>Joining with the Dur-Abzu</b> -<br /> <b>Corrupted</b>: The Joined develops new oblations, occult correspondences, and Path tools that reflect his journey through the Dur-Abzu. He begins with one new dedicated Path tool that symbolizes the betrayal at the heart of his Joining.<br /> <b>Abyssal Nimbus</b>: The mage gains a permanent version of the Abyssal Nimbus condition. This condition never lapses and cannot be scoured unless the mage severs her connection to the Dur-Abzu. Anything that would normally resolve this condition instead grants an Arcane Beat.<br /> <b>Paradox Control</b>: When rolling Gnosis to control Reach applied by Paradox, the roll gains the 8-Again Quality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Elder Diadem</b> -<br /> <b>Banking Paradox</b> - When a Paradox occurs within sensory range, the mage may reflexively spend Mana to 'store' successes on the Paradox roll, 1-for-1, reducing successes on the Paradox roll. If this reduces the number of successes below 1, no Paradox occurs.<br /> <b>Unleashing Paradox</b> - When a Paradox roll is made for any character within sensory range, the mage may reflexively release stored Paradox in order to increase the successes on the Paradox roll. All banked successes must be released at once - the mage cannot only release a fraction of his banked Paradox.<br /> <b>Abyssal Due</b> - All banked Paradox releases at the end of the scene in which it was banked if not Unleashed beforehand. The mage that banked the Paradox suffers the full effects of the Paradox. Rolls to contain this Paradox are made at a -2 penalty. This Paradox cannot be controlled via rolling Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Bonus Content for mages that somehow establish a Prelacy of the Gate:<br /> <br /> <b>The Crown of Lies</b><br /> The Gate grants the Crown of Lies. Whenever any mage within sensory range invokes a Paradox, a mage with the Crown of Lies may roll Gnosis to control the reach applied from the Paradox as if it were her own spell that prompted it. Also, she gains a bonus to invoking, banishing and negotiating with Abyssal entities equal to the dots she possesses in her highest Arcanum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-19-2016, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T06:08:33-07:00","id":917310,"title":"","content":"Definitely liking this. Especially the write-up for the Crown of Lies.<br /> <br /> Will be going with this until the devs release canon stuff for the Scelesti, as well as the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T06:51:14-07:00","id":917319,"title":"","content":"Excellent work so far.<br /> <br /> One idea I considered for the Nasnasi was that they gain Attainments based on their Abyssal Path, tied into their respective Untruths and Paradox in general.<br /> For instance, for Abyssal Mastigos I considered an Attainment that made it easier to cast powerful spells on yourself (afterall, in Drugaskan everyone <i>is </i>an island), while for Abyssal Thyrsus I considered something that broke the rules of they could use the Resonant and Open Conditions and how they could make Spirits use them (e.g. spending extra Reach to let a Spirit of Hate use a Friendship-resonant place as if it were Hatred-resonant).<br /> <br /> For the Crown of Lies, I would suggest a secondary effect, like for the other Crowns. I think the most apt would be a Highest Ruling Arcanum bonus to invoking, banishing and negotiating with Abyssal entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T06:55:05-07:00","id":917322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917307-rough-2e-conversion-of-scelesti-mechanics-from-left-hand-path?p=917319#post917319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent work so far.<br /> <br /> One idea I considered for the Nasnasi was that they gain Attainments based on their Abyssal Path, tied into their respective Untruths and Paradox in general.<br /> For instance, for Abyssal Mastigos I considered an Attainment that made it easier to cast powerful spells on yourself (afterall, in Drugaskan everyone <i>is </i>an island), while for Abyssal Thyrsus I considered something that broke the rules of they could use the Resonant and Open Conditions and how they could make Spirits use them (e.g. spending extra Reach to let a Spirit of Hate use a Friendship-resonant place as if it were Hatred-resonant).<br /> <br /> For the Crown of Lies, I would suggest a secondary effect, like for the other Crowns. I think the most apt would be a Highest Ruling Arcanum bonus to invoking, banishing and negotiating with Abyssal entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't even realized I neglected the second effect, good catch!<br /> <br /> And extra attainments based on Abyssal path would be an extremely awesome thing to see. Those examples are very creative.<br /> Edit: Added that as the secondary effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-19-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T13:06:40-07:00","id":1209753,"title":"","content":"I noticed that Dave has made a few more posts about how Scelesti work in 2E. <br /> <br /> I'm going to take some time to try and incorporate what makes sense here shortly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T01:18:51-07:00","id":1213357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917307-rough-2e-conversion-of-scelesti-mechanics-from-left-hand-path?p=1209753#post1209753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed that Dave has made a few more posts about how Scelesti work in 2E.<br /> <br /> I'm going to take some time to try and incorporate what makes sense here shortly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you link to these? I saw a post he made a while ago about stuff that was cut from the core, like about Scelesti replacing 'Wisdom' with 'Joining' but did he end up fleshing that out more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11057-sufferian","name":"sufferian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11057_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}